4 | // v3 SYSTEMATICALLY UNDERVALUED GROWTH COMPANIES. Two structural bugs, both now fixed:
5 | //   1. NO FADE. It dropped growth from 18% (MSFT) / 36% (NVDA) straight to the 3% terminal rate in
6 | //      year 6. Standard practice (Morningstar, McKinsey) fades growth over 10-15 years.
7 | //   2. TERMINAL CASH FLOW INHERITED THE GROWTH-YEAR DRAG: it did `terminal = lastFCF x (1+g)`, which
8 | //      permanently carries PEAK CAPEX and the huge working-capital investment required to FUND high
9 | //      growth. In steady state that investment collapses (NWC only funds ~3% growth, capex falls to
10 | //      maintenance). The terminal cash flow must be REBUILT, never scaled.
